# Oshiire configuration. Copy this file to `.env` and fill in the values.
# (Or leave all of this to the setup window: it writes the same keys to
# data/config.env. A value set here takes precedence and shows as "Set in .env".)
#
# ############################################################################
# #  WARNING -- `.env` CARRIES A SECRET. NEVER COMMIT OR SHARE IT.           #
# #                                                                          #
# #  REDDIT_SESSION_COOKIE is a logged-in browser cookie. Anyone who has it  #
# #  IS you on Reddit: it is not read-only and is not limited to your saves. #
# #                                                                          #
# #  Treat it exactly like a password: do not commit it, do not paste it     #
# #  into an issue, a chat, a screenshot, or a bug report, and do not let    #
# #  it into a log file.                                                     #
# #                                                                          #
# #  `.env` is gitignored, and this file (`.env.example`) is the only one    #
# #  of the pair that is committed -- keep it that way, and keep every       #
# #  value below EMPTY.                                                      #
# #                                                                          #
# #  If it does leak: log out of Reddit everywhere / change your Reddit      #
# #  password. That invalidates the cookie; then copy a fresh one.           #
# ############################################################################

# The root folder of your sorted archive -- where approved images are filed.
#
# It does NOT have to be an existing, organized archive: point it at an empty
# folder and the first `--apply` run creates the subfolders it needs. It can be
# a cloud-synced folder (Google Drive, OneDrive, Dropbox); Oshiire only ever
# moves files into it and lets the sync client do the upload. Use an absolute
# path. On Windows, either forward slashes or doubled backslashes are fine:
#   ARCHIVE_DIR=C:/Users/you/Google Drive/Art
ARCHIVE_DIR=

# Required for Ingest. Your Reddit username, without the u/ prefix. Ingest
# reads https://old.reddit.com/user/<this name>/saved/, so it must be the
# account the cookie below is logged in as. Also included in the User-Agent
# header of every request to Reddit, per Reddit's etiquette guidelines. Not a
# secret -- it is your public username.
REDDIT_USERNAME=

# Required for Ingest, and a SECRET.
#
# A logged-in cookie string copied from your browser. While logged in to
# old.reddit.com: devtools -> Network -> reload the page -> pick the "Doc"
# request -> Headers -> Request Headers -> copy the whole `Cookie:` value
# (without the word "Cookie:"). It must contain `reddit_session=`. Paste it as
# one line, in single quotes:
#   REDDIT_SESSION_COOKIE='reddit_session=<value>; token_v2=<value>; ...'
#
# Why it is needed: Reddit retired its RSS feeds on 2026-11-13, so Ingest now
# reads your saved list from the logged-in old.reddit page itself. Your saved
# list is private: without a valid cookie that page answers 403 "forbidden".
# Gallery posts (permalink fetch), the backfill CSV sweep and calibrate.py use
# the same cookie.
#
# The cookie is necessary but not sufficient: those fetches also go out over
# curl_cffi's Chrome-impersonated transport (installed by requirements.txt).
# You do not have to configure that part.
#
# IT EXPIRES. When Ingest stops with "Your Reddit login cookie has expired or
# is wrong", copy a fresh one the same way (or use the setup window's Test
# button to check it). Logging out or changing your password also ends it.
REDDIT_SESSION_COOKIE=

# No longer used: REDDIT_SAVED_FEED_URL (the RSS feed, retired by Reddit on
# 2026-11-13). An old value left in .env is ignored; you can delete the line.
